---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const components = [
  { name: 'Marketing site (acqi.tech)', what: 'These pages, served from Azure Static Web Apps.' },
  { name: 'Contact form delivery', what: 'The endpoint behind the contact form.' },
  { name: 'Preview gate', what: 'The shared-password gate in front of /preview.' },
  { name: 'Licence check service', what: 'The endpoint an installed product calls to validate a licence.' },
  { name: 'Update channel', what: 'Signed release packages for existing installations.' },
  { name: 'Support mailbox', what: 'Inbound mail to the support address.' },
];

const availability = [
  { name: 'Discovery collectors', state: 'Available', note: 'Microsoft 365, Entra ID, Azure, Active Directory, AWS and Google Cloud. Coverage differs per collector; ask for the current matrix.' },
  { name: 'Consolidated enterprise views', state: 'Available', note: 'People, applications, workspaces, sites, licensing and information systems with source attribution.' },
  { name: 'Organisation map', state: 'Available', note: 'Reporting lines and duplication between the two organisations.' },
  { name: 'Security and compliance assessment', state: 'Partial', note: 'Identity and exposure findings are in. Several control frameworks are still being mapped.' },
  { name: 'Migration planning', state: 'Available', note: 'Waves, mappings, runbooks and go/no-go.' },
  { name: 'Migration execution', state: 'Partial', note: 'User, mailbox, SharePoint, OneDrive, Teams, device and server workloads. Database and SaaS workload execution is in development.' },
  { name: 'Cloud Fit', state: 'Partial', note: 'Azure placement is usable. AWS and Google Cloud placement is in development.' },
  { name: 'Post-close operations', state: 'Partial', note: 'Day-one command and hypercare are in. The 100-day plan and synergy reconciliation are being rebuilt.' },
  { name: 'Aria Assist', state: 'Partial', note: 'Works against your own estate record. Actions that would change a production tenant are not enabled.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Status"
  description="Service status for acqi.tech. Nothing is monitored yet, and every row says so rather than showing a green light nothing measured."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1 reveal">Trust</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-2">Nothing on this page is green, because nothing is measured.</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-3">
        We have not built uptime monitoring yet. Rather than print a wall of green badges that
        no probe feeds, every row below says what it is. When a monitor exists, the row will
        show what it measured and over what window.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">I</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Service status</h2>
        <p class="micro section__note">Checked by hand · 17 November 2026</p>
      </div>

      <table class="table">
        <caption>Components</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Component</th>
            <th scope="col">What it covers</th>
            <th scope="col">State</th>
            <th scope="col">Basis</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {components.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{c.name}</th>
              <td>{c.what}</td>
              <td><span class="state state--none">Not monitored</span></td>
              <td class="small">No probe or synthetic check is configured for this component.</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="note mt-3">
        <p>
          <strong>What this means in practice.</strong> An outage would be discovered when
          someone tells us, not when a monitor fires. For a site of this size that is an
          acceptable risk, and saying so is more useful than a false assurance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">II</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Product availability</h2>
        <p class="micro section__note">Maintained by hand, reviewed each release</p>
      </div>

      <table class="table">
        <caption>What exists in current builds</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Capability</th>
            <th scope="col">State</th>
            <th scope="col">Detail</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {availability.map((a) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{a.name}</th>
              <td>
                <span class={a.state === 'Available' ? 'state' : 'state state--planned'}>{a.state}</span>
              </td>
              <td>{a.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p class="small mt-2 mb-0">
        Partial means some of the surface works and some of it does not. It is not a synonym for
        finished. Ask for the specific capability you need before you scope a deployment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">III</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Past incidents</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--sidebar">
        <p class="lede mb-0">No incidents recorded.</p>
        <div>
          <p class="mb-0">
            This page was published on 17 November 2026. There is no incident history before
            that date because there was no public service to have an incident on. If that
            changes, entries will be added here with a start time, an end time and a cause, and
            they will not be quietly removed later.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
